{"function": "main", "source": "// A complete Dart program implementing the Rabin-Karp string searching algorithm.\n// This script searches for a pattern in a given text and prints the starting indices of matches.\n\n@pragma('vm:entry-point')\nvoid main() {\n  // Example text and pattern\n  String text = \"ABABDABACDABABCABAB\";\n  String pattern = \"ABAB\";\n\n  // Parameters for hashing\n  int d = 256; // Number of characters in the input alphabet\n  int q = 101; // A prime number for modulo to avoid overflow\n\n  int n = text.length;\n  int m = pattern.length;\n\n  if (m > n) {\n    print(\"Pattern longer than text, no matches possible.\");\n    return;\n  }\n\n  // Precompute hash for pattern and first window of text\n  int patternHash = 0;\n  int textHash = 0;\n  int h = 1; // h = d^(m-1) % q\n\n  // Compute h\n  for (int i = 0; i < m - 1; i++) {\n    h = (h * d) % q;\n  }\n\n  // Compute initial hashes\n  for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {\n    patternHash = (d * patternHash + pattern.codeUnitAt(i)) % q;\n    textHash = (d * textHash + text.codeUnitAt(i)) % q;\n  }\n\n  // Slide the pattern over text one by one\n  bool found = false;\n  for (int i = 0; i <= n - m; i++) {\n    // If hashes match, check characters\n    if (patternHash == textHash) {\n      bool match = true;\n      for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) {\n        if (text[i + j] != pattern[j]) {\n          match = false;\n          break;\n        }\n      }\n      if (match) {\n        print(\"Pattern found at index $i\");\n        found = true;\n      }\n    }\n\n    // Compute hash for next window\n    if (i < n - m) {\n      textHash = (d * (textHash - text.codeUnitAt(i) * h) + text.codeUnitAt(i + m)) % q;\n      // Handle negative hash (in case modulo makes it negative)\n      if (textHash < 0) {\n        textHash += q;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  if (!found) {\n    print(\"No matches found.\");\n  }\n}", "assembly": "Dump of assembler code for function main:\n4\t@pragma('vm:entry-point')\n   0x000000000008